1,Western Tamang - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Western_Tamang,"Western Tamang, also known as Gyot Tamang, is a Tibeto-Burman language spoken by the Tamang people in Nepal. It belongs to the Tamangic branch within the Tamang languages, which is part of the Sino-Tibetan language family.","Tamang, Western",Sino-Tibetan
2,Tamang language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tamang_language,"Language family. Sino-Tibetan. Tamangic. Gurung–Tamang.Tamang (Devanagari: तामाङ; tāmāng) is a term used to collectively refer to a Sino-Tibetian language cluster spoken mainly in Nepal, Sikkim, West Bengal (Darjeeling) and North-Eastern India.","Tamang, Western",Sino-Tibetan
3,Tamang Language: A Guide and How to Learn It - World Schoolbooks,https://worldschoolbooks.com/tamang-language/,"Tamang is an essential part of Tamang cultural identity, oral tradition, and folklore. The language is used in daily conversation, traditional songs, ceremonies, and storytelling, making it an important medium for preserving the heritage of the Tamang community.","Tamang, Western",Sino-Tibetan
4,"Tamang, Western Language (TDG) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/tdg/,Western Tamang is a stable indigenous language of Nepal. It belongs to the Sino-Tibetan language family. The language is used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is taught as a subject of instruction in some schools.,"Tamang, Western",Sino-Tibetan
5,Western Tamang — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/western_tamang,"Western Tamang forms one of the primary clusters within the Tamangic branch of Tibeto-Burman languages, alongside Eastern Tamang, Central Tamang, and Southwestern Tamang varieties.","Tamang, Western",Sino-Tibetan
